commendation or hint is almost obvious  to mention which is  to separate production from  non-production environment  and while it sounds obvious it is  important to call out that  as you create your production pipelines  that run your  business process and business logic you  need to have  a separate environment to test the newly  created dacs or changes to those decks  separately from it and that's  particularly important because  not only you need to have management  separation but you also need to have  well fold domain separation as well as  management separation and  um performance and capacity separation  so for all those reasons you should have  at least two environments one for  production one for other  use cases obviously you can end up with  multiple environments for different  stages of your life cycle depending on  how your organizations  implement that one more item i would  like to call out in here is to also use  cacd so as the deployment process of dax  requires you to place dax into the  environment you want to make sure that  you control how this flow works  and there's a lot of different ways you  can establish ci cd pipeline  that leads to a proper dac deployment we  don't have a single solution as part of  our product but we have recommendations  in our website that you may want to look  into  on how to do it again there is not a  single solution because there is not a  single architecture that customers  follow  but again i highly encourage you to look  into the documentation that we have that  may help you establish those cicd  pipelines  for your specific use cases and one more  thing to  add in this specific scenario is while  you're having your separate environments  for different stages  please ensure you're using the same  versions of airflow and also have the  same versions of  dependent pi pi modules as otherwise the  testing may not be reliable enough  once you develop all of your dacs you  need to ensure that they run  successfully 